"notes": "GAAP village. Governmental receipts/disbursements from Exhibit E (labels p5, Total Governmental Funds 2025 column p6). Printed 'Taxes' 437,600 split into property tax 273,321 (General, p11) and sales tax 164,279 (General 120,859 + Street 43,420); 'Miscellaneous revenues' 10,851 split into rents 8,001 and misc 2,850 using the fund schedules. Principal and interest paid on long-term debt are printed under Other financing uses below Total expenditures, so recorded as disbursements with outside_printed_total; transfers in 373,097 and out 160,480 in their own fields (rolls forward: 2,003,437 + 853,933 - 1,523,645 - 148,178 + 373,097 - 160,480 = 1,398,164). Ending_cash computed from the governmental funds balance sheet (p4) as all cash, county treasurer cash and CDs including restricted; no beginning cash shown. Business-type: Exhibit H (p8) totals column: operating revenues + grant income + interest income as receipts; operating expenses (all categorized utilities) + interest expense as disbursements; transfers to other funds (212,617) in transfers_net; net position 2,408,305 -> 2,470,925. Grant income 7,000 categorized as donations/contributions (grantor not stated). Proprietary cash flow totals from p10 (Electric/Water/Sewer on p9). Balance sheet is government-wide Total column from Exhibit A (p1); due from/to other funds 87,811 shown in the totals as printed. Detail: General, Street, Fire fund schedules and the nonmajor combining statement (5 funds) recorded per fund; zero-amount lines omitted; Schedule 7 (accrual to cash basis reconciliation) and Schedule 8 (budget schedule, budget column shows dashes) not recorded as detail to avoid double counting; proprietary per-fund columns (Exhibit H) not repeated in detail. Read pages 1-17 of 17."
